# Group Arrival Register

Front office software for hotel group arrivals — rooming lists,
meal plans, room categories, occupancy control, printing and
operational reports.

**Version 1.0.0**

Built for front office staff who currently manage group arrivals
on paper registers and Excel sheets.

---

# Part 1 — For Front Office Staff

## What this software does

| Screen | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Dashboard** | Today's and tomorrow's arrivals, live totals, saved groups |
| **Arrival Register** | Enter a group — rooms, guests, pax, children, meals, VIP, requests |
| **Rooming List** | Automatic view of the open group for Housekeeping |
| **Room Master** | Map every room to a category and set occupancy limits |
| **Reports** | Live figures on screen, plus four printable reports |
| **Settings** | Hotel name, logo, register rules, manager PIN, backup |

## Before your first group — set up the Room Master

Nothing else works properly until this is done.

1. Go to **Room Master**
2. Under **Categories**, add each room type — Deluxe, Suite, and so on
3. For each category set:
   - **Default Adults** — auto-fills Pax when a room is typed
   - **Max Adults** — most adults allowed
   - **Max Children** — most children allowed
   - **Max Occupancy** — **total** people allowed in the room
4. Under **Add Rooms**, enter your rooms and pick a category:
   - `101` a single room
   - `101-110` a range
   - `101,105,107-109` a mixed list
5. Or use **Bulk Setup** — one line per entry:
   ```
   101-110,Deluxe
   201-206,Super Deluxe
   301,Suite
   ```

Max Occupancy is the total, and children count towards it. A
Deluxe with Max Occupancy 3 holds 2 adults + 1 child, or 3
adults — never 2 adults + 2 children.

## Entering a group

1. **Arrival Register**
2. Fill Group Name, Arrival Date, Agent and Prepared By
3. Enter the room count and click **Generate**
4. For each row:
   - Type the **Room** — the Category fills itself and Pax
     auto-fills from that category
   - Type the **Guest Name** — for a shared room put both
     names on one line: `Sharma, Rajesh + Sharma, Priya`
   - Adjust **Pax** if needed
   - Set **Children** if any — an age box appears for each
   - Choose the **Meal** plan
   - Tick **VIP** and add a Special Request if needed
5. Click **Save Group**

**Enter** moves down the same column, so you can type a whole
column without touching the mouse.

## Red cells mean Save is blocked

| Label | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `NOT IN MASTER` | That room is not in the Room Master |
| `DUPLICATE` | That room is already used in this group |
| `MAX n PAX` | More people than the room holds |
| `MAX n CHILD` | More children than the category allows |
| `MAX n ADULTS` | More adults than the category allows |

Fix every red cell before saving. Save will list every problem
if you try.

## If you clear or replace rows by mistake

**Clear Register**, **Generate Rows** and **Bulk Import** all
ask first when rows contain data, then show a blue bar:

> 38 row(s) replaced. The previous register can be restored
> until you leave this page.

Click **Restore** to get them back. This lasts until you leave
the page, so use it straight away.

## The unsaved draft banner

Your work is saved automatically about once a second. If the
browser closes or the power goes, the register comes back when
you reopen the app, with an amber bar:

> Unsaved draft restored.

**Keep** dismisses the message. **Discard** throws the recovered
work away. This is separate from Save Group — a restored draft
is not a saved group until you save it.

## Printing

**From the Arrival Register**
- **Print** — the arrival register for the group leader to sign
- **Blank** — an empty register for handwritten entry

**From the Rooming List**
- **Print Rooming List** — for Housekeeping, with VIP and
  special requests

**From Reports → Print Reports** — pick a date, pick a report:

| Report | For |
|---|---|
| **Daily Arrival Manifest** | Front office, duty manager |
| **Housekeeping Allocation** | Housekeeping |
| **Food & Beverage Covers** | Kitchen — includes breakfast, lunch and dinner counts |
| **Management Flash** | GM — date range, occupancy, agent business |

Room categories never appear on printed documents.

