# Part 2 — For IT and Installation

## Requirements

- A modern browser — Chrome, Edge or Firefox, updated within
  the last two years
- No internet connection required after installation
- No server, database or runtime to install
- Screen 1280×720 or larger

Not supported: Internet Explorer, or any browser with
JavaScript disabled.

## Installing

1. Copy the whole folder to the machine
2. Open `Group_Arrival_Register.html` in the browser
3. Create a desktop shortcut to that file

For a multi-machine setup, serve the folder over a local web
server. Note that **data does not sync between machines** —
each browser holds its own copy. Shared data arrives with the
database version.

## File structure

```
Group_Arrival_Register.html    the application
css/style.css                  all styling
js/
  dialog.js         in-page dialogs
  database.js       storage, migration, group repository
  printing.js       print engine and register documents
  room-master.js    room inventory, categories, occupancy, PIN
  register.js       arrival register, validation, capacity
  dashboard.js      KPIs, arrival cards, saved groups
  reports.js        on-screen reports
  report-print.js   printable operational reports
  groups.js         save, open, delete, import, export, autosave
  app.js            bootstrap, settings, navigation
  shortcuts.js      keyboard shortcuts
  diagnostics.js    health check
```

**Load order matters** and is fixed in the HTML. `dialog.js`
first, `database.js` second, `diagnostics.js` last.

## Where the data lives

Browser localStorage, keys `hotel_group_operations_v5` and
`GROUP_DRAFT`. Limit is roughly 5 MB — a few hundred groups.
Diagnostics warns at 75% and errors at 90%.

Backups are plain JSON and can be inspected in any text editor.

## Updating

Replace the changed file in `js/`, then increment the `?v=`
number on **every** script tag in the HTML so browsers reload
them. All twelve must carry the same number.

After updating, open the app and check the console for:

```
Suite Diagnostics — 10 modules, 0 problems, storage 0%
```

Any other result means the update did not apply cleanly.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Blank page, no buttons work | a JS file failed to load | check the console for a red error naming the file |
| Diagnostics reports missing functions | one file has a syntax error, or a script tag is missing | check the console for the parse error above it |
| Changes not appearing | browser cache | DevTools → Network → Disable cache, then reload |
| Column mismatch warning | HTML table headers do not match the code | do not use — restore the correct HTML |
| Save does nothing | storage full | take a backup, delete old groups |
| Print window does not open | pop-up blocker | allow pop-ups for this page |

## Known limits in version 1.0

- Single machine, single user — no sync or accounts
- No departure dates, so occupancy is measured on the arrival
  date only. A three-night group shows as occupying rooms for
  one day.
- No rates, so no revenue, ADR or RevPAR
- No housekeeping room status
- Manager PIN is an accident guard, not security
- One row is one room. Extra guests go in the Guest Name field
  as free text.

## Support

Run Settings → System Diagnostics first and have the output
ready. It reports module count, problems, storage use, groups
saved and rooms mapped.

